rogalacturonic acid, Sodium polypectate\nL82: \nL83: 【11†Sign In】 to View Organizational & Contract Pricing.\nL84: \nL85: ### Select a Size\nL86: \nL87: Change View\nL88: \nL89: Size/SKU  | Availability  | Price\nL90: --- | --- | ---\nL91: \nL92: * * *\nL93: ### About This Item\nL94: \nL95: CAS Number:\nL96: \nL97: 【12†9049-37-0】\nL98: \nL99: UNSPSC Code:\nL100: \nL101: 12352201\nL102: \nL103: NACRES:\nL104: \nL105: NA.25\nL106: \nL107: MDL number:\nL108: \nL109: 【13†MFCD00131975】\nL110: \nL111: eCl@ss:\nL112: \nL113: 39020601\nL114: \nL115: Pricing and availability is not currently available.\nL116: \nL117: Technical Service\nL118: \nL119: Need help? Our team of experienced scientists is here for you.\nL120: \nL121: 【14†Let Us Assist】\nL122: \nL123: * * *\nL124: \nL125: * * *\nL126: \nL127: Properties\nL128: \nL129: ### biological source\nL130: \nL131: citrus fruit\nL132: \nL133: ### Quality Segment\nL134: \nL135: 【15†200】\nL136: \nL137: ### assay\nL138: \nL139: ≥75% (titration)\nL140: \nL141: ### form\nL142: \nL143: powder\nL144: \nL145: ### color\nL146: \nL147: white to light brown\nL148: ### solubility\nL149: \nL150: water: 10 mg/mL, hazy to turbid, faintly yellow to yellow\nL151: \nL152: ### cation traces\nL153: \nL154: Na: 6.5-10.5% (ICP)\nL155: \nL156: ### storage temp.\nL157: \nL158: room temp\nL159: \nL160: Description\nL161: \nL162: ### General description\nL163: \nL164: Sodium polypectate sequesters metal ions and, in fungal cultures, it is used as a carbon source and inducer of polygalacturonases.\nL165: ### Application\nL166: \nL167: Sodium polypectate can be used to sequester metal ions. In fungal cultures, it is used as a carbon source and inducer of polygalacturonases.Polygalacturonic acid has been used in a study to assess an alkaline-active and alkali-stable pectate lyase from Streptomyces sp. S27 with potential in the textile industry. It has also been used in a study that investigated optimization of production and reaction conditions of polygalacturonase from Byssochlamys fulva.\nL168: ### Biochem/physiol Actions\nL169: \nL170: In land plants, polygalacturonic acids are major components of cell wall polysaccharides (pectins). Bound polygalacturonase-inhibiting peptides (PGIP) protect pectin from degradation by fungal polygalacturonases.\nL171: \nL172: ### Other Notes\nL173: \nL174: To gain a comprehensive understanding of our extensive range of 【16†Polysaccharides】 for your research, we encourage you to visit our 【17†Carbohydrates】 Category page.\nL175: \nL176: * * *\nL177: ## Compare Similar Items\nL178: \nL179: 【18†View Full Comparison】\nL180: \nL181: * * *\nL182: \nL183: Show Differences\nL184: \nL185: [Input]\nL186: \nL187: 1 of 1\nL188: ###### This Item\nL189:  | P3889  | 81325  | SMB00542\nL190: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL191: 【19†Sigma-Aldrich P3850 Polygalacturonic acid sodium salt】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich P3889 Polygalacturonic acid】[Button: Quick View]  | 【21†Sigma-Aldrich 81325 Polygalacturonic acid】[Button: Quick View]  | 【22†Sigma-Aldrich SMB00542 Polygalatenoside A】[Button: Quick View]\nL192: description from citrus fruit, ≥75% (titration)  | description≥85% (titration), from oranges  | description≥90% (enzymatic)  | description≥95% (LC/MS-ELSD)\nL193: biological source citrus fruit  | biological source oranges  | biological source synthetic  | biological source-\nL194: assay≥75% (titration)  | assay≥85% (titration)  | assay≥90% (enzymatic)  | assay≥95% (LC/MS-ELSD)\nL195: solubility water: 10 mg/mL, hazy to turbid, faintly yellow to yellow  | solubility aqueous NaOH: 1%, clear to hazy  | solubility-  | solubility DMSO: 1 mg/mL\nL196: Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 100  | Quality Level-\nL197: form powder  | form powder  | form powder  | form solid\nL198: storage temp.room temp  | storage temp.room temp  | storage temp.room temp  | storage temp.−20°C\nL199: * * *\nL200: ## Safety Information\nL201: \nL202: ### Storage Class\nL203: \nL204: 11 - Combustibl